From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:05:50 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] color-device: Apply ramps the CRTC cannot take in the
 compositor

Without a CRTC gamma LUT, a client ramp was approximated by a CTM of its
white point, ICC VCGT curves were not applied at all, and outputs with
neither a gamma LUT nor a CTM got no night light and no client ramp.

Pick the path per update:
- a CRTC gamma LUT: program it (unchanged);
- else a ramp that is a straight line per channel (night light without
  VCGT, gamma-control temperature and brightness ramps) and a CTM: the
  diagonal CTM (unchanged, exact for those);
- else (curved or offset client ramp, VCGT, or no CTM): hand the ramp
  to the renderer views of the device, which apply it in their final
  blit, and put the CTM back to identity.

An identity ramp never enables the blit. Views with a ramp block direct
scanout and inhibit the hardware cursor plane, which would skip it.
Views whose CRTC is gone (monitors being rebuilt) ignore the change;
their replacements take the ramp when they are created. The
gamma-control ramp size is now offered on every active monitor without
a gamma LUT, and night light is reported as supported on every CRTC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
